{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2179-11-10 12:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you came in with a headache today. How are you feeling now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2179-11-10 12:22:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. The headache started after my dialysis yesterday, behind my left eye. It’s the same one I always get. I usually take Percocet, but I ran out."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2179-11-10 12:23:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You mentioned it’s a recurring pain. Is it usually this bad when you don’t have medication?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2179-11-10 12:24:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, pretty much. Tylenol doesn’t help. I’ve been coming to the ER when it gets like this. Last time, they gave me Percocet and sent me home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2179-11-10 12:25:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Got it. We checked your labs and found something important — your potassium level was high, at 5.9. That can be dangerous for the heart."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2179-11-10 12:26:05",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "High potassium? I didn’t feel any heart issues. Should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2179-11-10 12:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re being cautious. Your ECG showed some changes — slightly peaked T waves — which can happen with high potassium. We gave you calcium gluconate and kayexalate in the ER to bring it down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2179-11-10 12:28:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. Did it work?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2179-11-10 12:28:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your repeat potassium came back at 5.1, which is much better. But we want to keep an eye on it, especially since you’re on dialysis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2179-11-10 12:29:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had dialysis yesterday. Shouldn’t that have taken care of my potassium?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2179-11-10 12:30:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It should help, but sometimes levels can rise between sessions, especially if there’s constipation or if your phosphate binders aren’t taken with meals."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2179-11-10 12:31:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been regular with my meds. But I’ve had diarrhea since the kayexalate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2179-11-10 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a common side effect. It should settle soon. We’ll monitor your levels tonight and tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2179-11-10 12:32:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my headache? Can I get something for that again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2179-11-10 12:33:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We gave you Percocet earlier, and the nurse said your pain improved. Is it still bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2179-11-10 12:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It’s better now, thanks. But why does this keep happening? I’m blind in that eye already."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2179-11-10 12:35:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Even without vision, the eye can still have pain. Given your history, this could be related to glaucoma. We recommend following up with your eye doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2179-11-10 12:36:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t been in a while. Maybe I should make an appointment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2179-11-10 12:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that would be a good idea. For now, we’ll keep you here overnight for monitoring because of the potassium issue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2179-11-10 12:37:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. What about my regular dialysis? It’s scheduled for tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2179-11-10 12:38:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll do your dialysis here tomorrow as planned. That should help keep your potassium and other levels in check."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2179-11-10 12:39:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. And my other meds — should I take them tonight?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2179-11-10 12:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve reviewed your list. You’ll get your usual doses, including insulin, blood pressure meds, and warfarin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2179-11-10 12:40:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My Coumadin levels were low last time. Should we check that again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2179-11-10 12:41:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we checked it — it was low again. We’ll adjust your dose and have it rechecked at your next dialysis session."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2179-11-10 12:42:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thank you. I don’t want to have a stroke."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2179-11-10 12:43:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re making sure of that. You’re on good medications to prevent that. Just keep taking them as directed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2179-11-11 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your potassium this morning is 4.1 — that’s normal. Great improvement."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2179-11-11 08:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good news! Any more ECG changes?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2179-11-11 08:17:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The peaked T waves are still there slightly, but your levels are stable, and you’ve had no symptoms. We think it’s resolving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2179-11-11 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my headache?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2179-11-11 08:18:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve been pain-free since yesterday. That’s a good sign. We’ll give you a prescription for oxycodone with acetaminophen to use as needed at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2179-11-11 08:19:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "How many can I take?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2179-11-11 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One every six hours as needed, but not more than four in 24 hours. And don’t take it with other pain meds unless we say so."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2179-11-11 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. What about my sevelamer? I know I need to take it with food."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2179-11-11 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and we’re switching you to sevelamer HCl — two tablets with each meal. It works better with your current labs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2179-11-11 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll do that. And I’ll keep up with my eye drops too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2179-11-11 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You just finished your dialysis session. Everything went smoothly. We’re planning to discharge you this afternoon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2179-11-11 12:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. Any final instructions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2179-11-11 12:17:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep taking all your meds, especially Coumadin. Get your INR checked at your next dialysis. Follow up with your primary doctor and eye specialist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2179-11-11 12:18:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if the headache comes back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2179-11-11 12:19:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Use the new prescription as directed. If it’s severe or different, or if you have chest pain, weakness, or shortness of breath, come back right away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2179-11-11 12:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you, Doctor. I feel much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2179-11-11 12:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll get your discharge papers ready. Take care."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2179-11-10 12:21:00",
    "admission_end": "2179-11-11 17:45:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 68-year-old female with end-stage renal disease, diabetes, atrial fibrillation, and chronic diastolic heart failure was admitted due to a headache and incidentally found hyperkalemia with a potassium level of 5.9 and ECG changes. She was treated with calcium gluconate and kayexelate, resulting in potassium normalization to 4.1. Her headache, a chronic issue related to left eye pain, resolved with oxycodone-acetaminophen. She underwent an inpatient hemodialysis session without complications. Warfarin dosing was adjusted due to subtherapeutic INR, and discharge medications were updated, including a change to sevelamer HCl. She was discharged home in stable condition with instructions to follow up with her primary care provider and ophthalmologist.",
    "problems": [
      "Hyperpotassemia",
      "Headache",
      "Hypertensive chronic kidney disease, unspecified, with chronic kidney disease stage V or end stage renal disease",
      "End stage renal disease",
      "Diabetes mellitus without mention of complication, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Long-term (current) use of insulin",
      "Atrial fibrillation",
      "Long-term (current) use of anticoagulants",
      "Peripheral vascular disease, unspecified",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Below knee amputation status",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Unspecified glaucoma",
      "Tobacco use disorder",
      "Chronic diastolic heart failure",
      "Congestive heart failure, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
